WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:14.581
This is the story of the Darling family.

2
00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:22.612
It is also the story of Peter Pan, a boy who may or may not exist—depending on how old you are.

3
00:00:22.613 --> 00:00:29.335
The Darlings lived at Number 14, a house in London, England, near Kensington Gardens.

4
00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:34.227
At first, the family was just Mr. George Darling and his wife, Mrs. Darling.

5
00:00:34.228 --> 00:00:36.566
But then their children were born.

6
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:41.072
Wendy came first, then John, and then Michael.

7
00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:45.157
Later, Nana came to live with them.

8
00:00:45.158 --> 00:00:50.011
She was the children's nanny and made sure they were all well-cared for.

9
00:00:50.012 --> 00:00:56.060
Nana was a large, no-nonsense Newfoundland dog, who slept on the nursery floor.

10
00:00:56.061 --> 00:00:59.549
Mr. Darling was a good father and an excellent provider.

11
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:06.263
During the day, he worked in the city as a banker, encouraging people to spend money wisely.

12
00:01:06.264 --> 00:01:09.523
He liked to work with numbers at home too.

13
00:01:09.524 --> 00:01:13.200
Mr. Darling counted how much money the children cost him.

14
00:01:13.201 --> 00:01:16.851
How much would he have to spend on their milk and cookies?

15
00:01:16.852 --> 00:01:20.784
How much money would he spend on their shirts and coats?

16
00:01:20.785 --> 00:01:26.623
When the children caught the German measles or the mumps, he worried about the cost of medicine.

17
00:01:26.624 --> 00:01:32.329
But he and Mrs. Darling agreed that the children were worth every penny spent.

18
00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:37.239
Mrs. Darling was more concerned about her children’s minds than about money.

19
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.989
She was a lovely lady with a sweet mouth and a romantic sense of the world.

20
00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:48.205
Her mind was like a puzzle with many boxes, each one inside the other.

21
00:01:48.206 --> 00:01:51.008
Mrs. Darling thought about deep things.

22
00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:54.167
She worried about how her children were growing up.

23
00:01:54.168 --> 00:02:02.288
She knew from her own experience that when a child reaches the age of two, childhood is beginning to end.

24
00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:06.287
As a young girl, Mrs. Darling had many suitors.

25
00:02:06.288 --> 00:02:08.833
All of them wanted to marry her.

26
00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:13.739
But George Darling, who was a young man at the time, asked her first.

27
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.765
He was very smart.

28
00:02:15.766 --> 00:02:24.211
One day, while the other boys were walking to her house to propose, Mr. Darling took a taxi.

29
00:02:24.212 --> 00:02:27.335
He got there ahead of the others and won her love.

30
00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:31.450
She happily gave him all her kisses, except for one.

31
00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.440
This kiss was her little secret.

32
00:02:34.441 --> 00:02:39.296
She saved it in the right corner of her sweet mouth for a special occasion.

33
00:02:39.297 --> 00:02:43.678
When Mrs. Darling was busy, Nana took care of the children.

34
00:02:43.679 --> 00:02:45.954
Nana was a treasure.

35
00:02:45.955 --> 00:02:51.909
Every morning, she walked the children in single file to Miss Fulsom’s kindergarten school.

36
00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:56.189
When they were well-behaved, Nana walked quietly by their side.

37
00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:02.509
When they were naughty, she barked and pushed them back into line with her huge head.

38
00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:07.357
She always carried an umbrella in her mouth, just in case of rain.

39
00:03:07.358 --> 00:03:12.224
Mr. Darling hired Nana as a nanny because she was much cheaper than a person.

40
00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:20.256
Even though the neighbors might gossip about a dog working as a nanny, the idea made perfect sense to Mr. Darling.

41
00:03:20.257 --> 00:03:25.701
Before Nana picked up the children from school, she waited in the basement with the other nannies.

42
00:03:25.702 --> 00:03:32.901
They complained about having a dog among them, and the neighbors did talk, but the Darlings didn't care.

43
00:03:32.902 --> 00:03:37.915
Before bedtime, there was always much merriment at Number 14.

44
00:03:37.916 --> 00:03:41.877
The children were allowed to sing and dance before going to bed.

45
00:03:41.878 --> 00:03:47.306
Oh, the dances were such fun! Nana barked in time with the music.

46
00:03:47.307 --> 00:03:51.172
The other servant, Liza, danced too.

47
00:03:51.173 --> 00:03:55.639
Mr. Darling watched alone and apart on the sidelines.

48
00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.544
But Mrs. Darling joined the children and spun around wildly.

49
00:03:59.545 --> 00:04:04.950
And sometimes she even planted her secret kiss on the cheek of one of the children.

50
00:04:04.951 --> 00:04:15.933
Yes, the Darling family lived very happily together—until the coming of Peter Pan.
